d":790},{"pmid":"16820346","text":"dex","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D003907","start":793,"end":796},{"pmid":"16820346","text":"nitrate","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D009566","start":818,"end":825},{"pmid":"16820346","text":"nitrite","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D009573","start":826,"end":833},{"pmid":"16820346","text":"dex","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D003907","start":857,"end":860},{"pmid":"16820346","text":"Atorva","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"C065179","start":976,"end":982},{"pmid":"16820346","text":"atorvastatin","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"C065179","start":1036,"end":1048},{"pmid":"16820346","text":"dexamethasone","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D003907","start":1072,"end":1085},{"pmid":"16820346","text":"hypertension","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D006973","start":1094,"end":1106}],"gold_relations":"dexamethasone | CID | hypertension","metrics":{"precision":0.16666666666666666,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.2857142857142857,"tp":1,"fp":5,"fn":0,"rel_precision":0.16666666666666666,"rel_recall":1.0,"rel_f1":0.2857142857142857,"rel_tp":1,"rel_fp":5,"rel_fn":0},"pmid":"16820346","relations":["D000069059 | CID | D003907","D003907 | CID | D009566","D003907 | CID | D009573","D003915 | CID | D013481","D003907 | CID | D006973","D000069059 | CID | D006973"],"text":"Atorvastatin prevented and reversed dexamethasone-induced hypertension in the rat. To assess the antioxidant effects of atorvastatin (atorva) on dexamethasone (dex)-induced hypertension, 60 male Sprague-Dawley rats were treated with atorva 30 mg/kg/day or tap water for 15 days. Dex increased systolic blood pressure (SBP) from 109 +/- 1.8 to 135 +/- 0.6 mmHg and plasma superoxide (5711 +/- 284.9 saline, 7931 +/- 392.8 U/ml dex, P < 0.001). In this prevention study, SBP in the atorva + dex group was increased from 115 +/- 0.4 to 124 +/- 1.5 mmHg, but this was significantly lower than in the dex-only group (P' < 0.05). Atorva reversed dex-induced hypertension (129 +/- 0.6 mmHg, vs. 135 +/- 0.6 mmHg P' < 0.05) and decreased plasma superoxide (7931 +/- 392.8 dex, 1187 +/- 441.2 atorva + dex, P < 0.0001). Plasma nitrate/nitrite (NOx) was decreased in dex-treated rats compared to saline-treated rats (11.2 +/- 1.08 microm, 15.3 +/- 1.17 microm, respectively, P < 0.05). Atorva affected neither plasma NOx nor thymus weight. Thus, atorvastatin prevented and reversed dexamethasone-induced hypertension in the rat."}